.TH _PRINTF 3 "August 2026" "Holberton Coding School" "C Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
_printf \- formatted output conversion function
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"
.PP
.BI "int _printf(const char *" format ", ...);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B _printf()
function produces output according to a format string, writing to standard output.
.SS Format Specifiers
A conversion specifier is introduced by the '%' character:
.TP
.B %c
Prints a single ASCII character.
.TP
.B %s
Prints a null-terminated string. If pointer is NULL, prints "(null)".
.TP
.B %%
Prints a literal '%' character.
.TP
.B %d, %i
Prints a signed decimal integer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters printed. Returns -1 if the format string is NULL or if a trailing '%' is encountered.
